Done. **`/workspace/output/repurpose.mp4`** — 75.000s, 720×1280, H.264 High + AAC, ~20MB, faststart-ready for Instagram.
**The cut:**
| Time | Beat |
|---|---|
| 0:00–0:08 | Ryan Castle — "Hello everybody, welcome inside AT&T Stadium, I'm Ryan Castle... Jesse Holley, former Dallas Cowboys receiver" — the reel opens in the building, no bumper |
| 0:08–0:21 | Establish: "stars are going to be born here in the home of the star," Holley on playing these stadiums as a dream come true, "the kickoff from AT&T Stadium is coming right up" |
| 0:21–0:31 | **Beat 1 — the pick six**: live call, "It is. It's a touchdown. A pick six for Team East, Nick Don Vito" → 7–0 |
| 0:31–0:40 | "Seven-to-nothing lead" + kickoff **huge hit** — East's statement |
| 0:40–0:50 | **WEST's breath** — Evan Dameron's open-field tackle, given air so it doesn't read one-sided |
| 0:50–0:57 | **Beat 2 — 39-yd FG**, goalpost-framed → 10–0 |
| 0:57–1:08 | **Beat 3 — 49-yd FG** "what a weapon" → 13–0 |
| 1:08–1:13 | "Team East continues their dominant special teams play" — pace tightens into the close |
| 1:13–1:15 | End card: **SCORE 13–0**, EAST/WEST shields, Blue Grey × AT&T Stadium, "EAST TAKES COMMAND AT THE STAR" |
**How it was built:** Whisper (base) transcribed the full 14-min broadcast to timestamp every scoring beat, then ffmpeg laid each beat onto a blurred-fill vertical canvas (full broadcast frame kept — the score bug, the star, the endzones all stay in frame), with short audio fades giving each beat its breath. The scoreboard only moves one direction: 7 → 10 → 13, and the card leaves it exactly where the broadcast left it.
